  "note": "12C has I = 0, so A has no effect and the spectrum is the g-only powder pattern; the case checks that a spin-0 nucleus is accepted and ignored. Sys.A = [50 400] (axial, MHz). pepper's projection step (no strains) returns ref[i] ~ true(x[i] + dx/2): an independent converged powder sum matched axiallw, rhombiclw, ordering_axial row 0, pt_gonly, iso_12c and modamp best with the simulator evaluated at x + 0.5*dx (residual 4e-4 to 9e-3 there, 3e-2 to 2.7e-1 at x). The g-strain case (pepper's summation path) needs no offset.",
